# The sim's behaviour as a keyboard pilot sees it, standalone (no ArduPilot), flying the plain
# T1-S, which has no flight controller. Each event is
# a key press and each state is read from the live sim: see src/acceptance.rs. Events and
# phrases say what the pilot means ("throws the plane"); their Say: lines give the keys.

Section: The simulator
  Fly the T1-S Ranger from the [[pilot box]] at the field. Throw it, fly it from the
  keyboard, and pick it up again. Start with [[Your first throw]].

  On the keyboard, W and S move the nose down and up. A and D roll the plane, and Q and E
  move the rudder. Shift opens the throttle and Ctrl closes it. The keys 1 to 5 set the
  throttle to 20, 40, 60, 80 or 100 %, and 0 closes it. Press H at any time to see all the
  keys. The [[HUD]] on the view shows the flight mode, the view and all the readings.

Vocabulary:
  State: the throttle is 0..100 %
    Set: set the throttle to {value} with Shift, or with the number keys
    Shows: the THR reading on the HUD is {value}%
  State: the pitch stick is forward | centred | back
    Set: hold the pitch stick {value}
  State: the roll stick is left | centred | right
  State: the wings are level | banked
    Shows: banked: the plane banks, and the roll reading on the ATT line of the HUD moves away from 0
    Shows: level: the wings become level, and the roll reading on the ATT line of the HUD goes back to near 0
  State: the flight controller is fitted | missing
    Shows: missing: the plane has only a receiver and two ESCs, so the sticks move the control surfaces directly
  State: the flight mode is MANUAL | ANGLE | ACRO
    Set: press M on the keyboard until the flight mode is {value}
    Shows: the top line of the HUD starts with {value}
  State: the rates are low | high
    Set: press L for {value} rates
    Shows: the top line of the HUD says {value} rates
  State: differential thrust is on | off
    Set: press X to turn differential thrust {value}
    Shows: the top line of the HUD says diff thrust {value}
  State: the view is line of sight | chase | FPV
    Set: press C until the view is {value}
    Shows: line of sight: you see the plane from the pilot box again, and the HUD says CAM LINE OF SIGHT
    Shows: chase: the view follows the plane from behind, and the HUD says CAM CHASE
    Shows: FPV: you see the picture from the nose camera of the plane, and the HUD says CAM FPV
  State: auto-zoom is on | off
    Set: press Z to turn auto-zoom {value}
    Shows: on: the CAM line on the HUD says (auto-zoom) again, and the view zooms to keep the plane in sight
    Shows: off: (auto-zoom) goes away from the CAM line on the HUD, and the zoom stays the same
  State: the help screen is shown | hidden
    Shows: shown: the help screen appears on the view
    Shows: hidden: the help screen goes away
  State: the sim is running | paused
    Shows: paused: everything stops, and the HUD says PAUSED (P)
    Shows: running: PAUSED (P) goes away, and the flight continues from the point where it stopped
  State: the battery is 0..100 %
    Shows: at least 99 %: the BAT reading on the HUD is approximately 100 % again
  # The games of the Recreation section. Without one, you fly freely.
  State: the game is free flight | a race | tag
    Shows: free flight: the game panel, the pylons and the other planes go away
    Shows: a race: three tall pylons stand on the field, and the game panel says RACE
    Shows: tag: the game panel says TAG
  State: the game clock is off | counting down | running | stopped
    Shows: off: the game panel goes away
    Shows: counting down: all the planes go back to the hands of their pilots, and the game panel counts down to GO
    Shows: running: the game panel says GO, and its clock starts
    Shows: stopped: the clock on the game panel stops, and the game panel shows the results

  Event: the pilot throws the plane
    Say: press Space to throw the plane
  Event: the pilot resets the plane
    Say: press R
  Event: the pilot changes flight mode
    Say: press M on the keyboard
  Event: the pilot changes rates
    Say: press L
  Event: the pilot toggles differential thrust
    Say: press X
  Event: the pilot changes the view
    Say: press C
  Event: the pilot toggles auto-zoom
    Say: press Z
  Event: the pilot toggles the help
    Say: press H
  Event: the pilot closes the help
    Say: press Esc
  Event: the pilot toggles pause
    Say: press P
  Event: the pilot fits a fresh battery
    Say: press V

  Phrase: the sim has just started
    Say: install Rust. Then run `cargo run --release -- --aircraft t1s-ranger` in the repository. The sim opens at the pilot box with the plain T1-S, which has no flight controller. The plane is in your hand, the throttle is closed and the flight mode is MANUAL
    Given the flight controller is missing
    And the plane is in hand
    And the throttle is 0 %
    And the pitch stick is centred
    And the roll stick is centred
    And the wings are level
    And the flight mode is MANUAL
    And the rates are high
    And differential thrust is on
    And the view is line of sight
    And auto-zoom is on
    And the help screen is hidden
    And the sim is running
    And the battery is at least 99 %
    And the game is free flight
    And the game clock is off

  Phrase: the pilot throws the plane with the throttle
    Say: press 4 to set the throttle to 80 %
    When the throttle is 80 %

  Phrase: the pilot closes the throttle
    Say: press 0 to close the throttle
    When the throttle is 0 %

  Phrase: the pilot throws the plane nose-down
    Say: hold W to push the nose down, and at the same time press 5 for full throttle
    When the pitch stick is forward
    And the throttle is 100 %

  Phrase: the pilot lets go and closes the throttle
    Say: release W. Then press 0 to close the throttle
    When the pitch stick is centred
    And the throttle is 0 %

  Phrase: the pilot rolls the plane to the left
    Say: hold A to roll the plane to the left
    When the roll stick is left

  Phrase: the pilot releases the roll stick
    Say: release A
    When the roll stick is centred

Background:
  Given the sim has just started
